  "notes": "PATTERN B -- no University Park equivalent (confirmed in SWENG-2026.json notes). Built from Penn State Behrend's 2023-24 Suggested Academic Plan and 'Requirements for the Major' course table (fetched via bulletin_scraper.py 2023 2026). All required courses and credit values match the scraper's linked_codes output. Real prereq-chain workarounds applied (same as SWENG-2026.json): (1) MATH 21/22 remediation sequence added to unlock downstream math courses (bulletin assumes test-out); (2) CMPSC 221 added in Semester 6 purely to unlock CMPSC 431W/461 prereqs. This extends the plan to 9 semesters (4.5 years), registered with grad_years=5 to match actual curricular load, same as 2026. REVIEWER #4 FIX (2026-09-18): Semester 2 was missing CAS 100 entirely (item-credit sum 11 vs stated target_credits 14, a 3cr gap) -- the bulletin never hyperlinks a specific CAS 100 section in any catalog year (confirmed via bulletin_scraper.py for 2022-2026 archives: text-only \"CAS 100\" with no <a> tag, except a stray unverifiable link in the 2022 archive specifically), so it was apparently dropped during the MATH-remediation semester reshuffle instead of being carried into the new semester order. Added back as a literal CAS 100A/100B/100C course choice (3cr) in Semester 2, matching SWENG-2026.json's own established modeling of this identical bulletin item. Verified: item-credit sum now matches target_credits exactly, and build_full_plan still completes in 9 terms with zero warnings. REVIEWER #4 FIX #2 (2026-09-18): Semester 6 (formerly target_credits 15.5, items summing to only 13.5) was missing SWENG 411 (Software Engineering, 3cr) -- a real, required course per this app's own sweng_catalog.json entry ('Required course per the Software Engineering, B.S. bulletin') and confirmed present as a literal linked course in the raw bulletin Suggested Academic Plan (all archived years 2022-2026 alike, via bulletin_scraper.py) -- that was silently dropped when CMPSC 221 was added to this semester for its own prereq-unlock reason, rather than being moved elsewhere. Added SWENG 411 back into Semester 6 (room existed under the 17cr/semester cap: 13.5 + 3 = 16.5), corrected target_credits from 15.5 to 16.5. Verified: item-credit sum now matches target_credits, and build_full_plan still completes in 9 terms with zero warnings. REVIEWER #4 FIX #3 (2026-09-18): MATH 220 (Matrices, 2cr, real course, prereq MATH 140/110-or-equivalent already satisfied by Semester 3 in this plan) was completely absent from the whole plan despite being a required, linked course in the raw bulletin's own Suggested Academic Plan (Spring Year 1 in every archived year 2022-2026, confirmed via bulletin_scraper.py) -- an omission of the same kind as SWENG 411 above, not something the notes ever flagged as an intentional substitution. Added to Semester 4, which had room (13 + 2 = 15, under the 17cr/semester cap) and comes after both MATH 140 (Semester 1) and MATH 110 (Semester 3), either of which satisfies its prereq.",
